  tip What 60-105 takes that the Auction House sells: 247 Light Leather and 20 Medium Hide. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2318 x247
  auction 4232 x20

step Leatherworking 60-105: skinning
  tip Light Leather comes from beasts of level 1-15; Medium Hides from beasts of level 18-30. Take them from your bags or bank after the skinning loops above.
  collect 2318 x247 anywhere gather Skinning 1
  collect 4232 x20 anywhere gather Skinning 80

step Embossed Leather Pants (60-80)
  tip Embossed Leather Pants, 20 to 80: 1 Cured Light Hide, 6 Light Leather and 2 Coarse Thread each. These take the 20 Cured Light Hides kept from the last band. Without them, make 24 more Embossed Leather Gloves (72 Light Leather, 48 Coarse Thread) instead.
  learn 3759 "Embossed Leather Pants"
  craft 3759 "Embossed Leather Pants" until 80

step Cured Medium Hide (80-95)
  tip Cured Medium Hide, 20 to 95: 1 Medium Hide and 1 Salt each. Keep all 20 for the Dark Leather Belts at 105. Without Medium Hides, make 19 Fine Leather Belts (114 Light Leather, 38 Coarse Thread) instead.
  learn 3817 "Cured Medium Hide"
  craft 3817 "Cured Medium Hide" until 95

step Fine Leather Belt (95-105)
  tip Fine Leather Belt, 22 to 105: 6 Light Leather and 2 Coarse Thread each. Keep 20 of the belts for the Dark Leather Belts at 105.
  learn 3763 "Fine Leather Belt"
  craft 3763 "Fine Leather Belt" until 105

section Leatherworking 105-150

step Skin the Raptors (Barrens)
  only Horde
  zone The Barrens
  tip Stay in the raptor camp west of Northwatch Hold until Skinning 150; the last points come slowly but the camp refills fast. Heavy Hides and Medium Leather from here feed the next two Leatherworking bands. Horde can also pick up the Keen Skinning Knife (+3 Skinning) from the Unwelcome Guests quest in the Barrens.
  goto 61.3,47.8 "Ornery Plainstrider" r 30
  goto 48.8,47.4 "Ornery Plainstrider, Zhevra Charger" r 30
  goto 48.1,50.3 "Sunscale Scytheclaw" r 30
  goto 52.8,51.6 "Sunscale Scytheclaw, Zhevra Charger" r 30
  skill Skinning 150

step Skin the Raptors (Wetlands)
  only Alliance
  zone Wetlands
  tip Mottled Scytheclaws and Mottled Razormaws (level 25-27) gather around Whelgar's Excavation Site in the north of the Wetlands. At Skinning 130 you can skin the 25s; the 26s and 27s open up as you climb. Work to Skinning 150, keeping every Medium Leather and Heavy Hide.
  goto 34.7,49.8 "Mottled Scytheclaw, Mottled Razormaw" r 30
  goto 36.0,48.4 "Mottled Scytheclaw" r 30
  goto 34.2,46.5 "Mottled Razormaw, Mottled Scytheclaw" r 30
  goto 31.7,48.5 "Mottled Scytheclaw, Mottled Razormaw" r 30
  skill Skinning 150

step Expert Skinning
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Expert Skinning raises the cap to 225 and needs skill 125. Balthus Stoneflayer in Ironforge teaches it.
  train Skinning Expert npc 6291

step Expert Skinning
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Expert Skinning raises the cap to 225 and needs skill 125. Thuwd in Orgrimmar teaches it.
  train Skinning Expert npc 7088

step Skin the Foothill Caverns Approach
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip Vicious Gray Bears and Starving Mountain Lions (level 22-24) prowl the slopes in front of the Foothill Caverns in northern Hillsbrad. Work them to Skinning 160, then take the yetis inside up to Skinning 175. Horde come from Tarren Mill, Alliance from Southshore. Heavy Hides and Heavy Leather from here and the next stretch are what the 130-175 crafts need.
  goto 53.0,37.7 "Starving Mountain Lion, Vicious Gray Bear" r 30
  goto 41.5,42.6 "Vicious Gray Bear, Starving Mountain Lion" r 30
  goto 43.3,31.2 "Cave Yeti, Ferocious Yeti" r 30
  goto 45.2,28.4 "Ferocious Yeti" r 30
  skill Skinning 175

step Leatherworking 105-150: vendor goods
  tip Fine Thread (72) for the belts and gloves, Gray Dye (20) for the belts, and Salt (75) for the Cured Heavy Hides, from any Leatherworking Supply vendor.
  buy 2321 x72 nearest
  buy 4340 x20 nearest
  buy 4289 x75 nearest

step Leatherworking 105-150: Auction House
  tip What 105-150 takes that the Auction House sells: 147 Medium Leather and 25 Heavy Hide. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2319 x147
  auction 4235 x25

step Leatherworking 105-150: skinning
  tip Medium Leather and Heavy Hides come from beasts of level 18-40. Take them from your bags or bank after the skinning loops above.
  collect 2319 x147 anywhere gather Skinning 80
  collect 4235 x25 anywhere gather Skinning 140

step Dark Leather Belt (105-125)
  tip Dark Leather Belt, 20 to 125: 1 Fine Leather Belt, 1 Cured Medium Hide, 2 Fine Thread and 1 Gray Dye each. These take the 20 belts and 20 hides kept from the last band. Without the hides, make 16 Dark Leather Pants (192 Medium Leather, 16 Gray Dye, 16 Fine Thread) to 120, then 5 Hillman's Leather Gloves (70 Medium Leather, 20 Fine Thread) to 125 instead.
  learn 3766 "Dark Leather Belt"
  craft 3766 "Dark Leather Belt" until 125

step Heavy Leather (125-130)
  tip Heavy Leather, 7 to 130: 5 Medium Leather each. No Tanning Rack is needed here: the Rack is a camp item (skill 125, blueprint from Razorclaw the Butcher in Shadowfang Keep), not a gate on this step.
  learn 20649 "Heavy Leather"
  craft 20649 "Heavy Leather" until 130

step Cured Heavy Hide (130-143)
  tip Cured Heavy Hide, 25 to 143: 1 Heavy Hide and 3 Salt each. Keep them all: 15 go to the Barbaric Shoulders at 150 and 10 to the Guardian Gloves at 165. Without Heavy Hides, skip them and make Hillman's Leather Gloves from 130 to 150 instead (21 of them: 294 Medium Leather, 84 Fine Thread).
  learn 3818 "Cured Heavy Hide"
  craft 3818 "Cured Heavy Hide" until 143

step Hillman's Leather Gloves (143-150)
  tip Hillman's Leather Gloves, 8 to 150: 14 Medium Leather and 4 Fine Thread each.
  learn 3764 "Hillman's Leather Gloves"
  craft 3764 "Hillman's Leather Gloves" until 150

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert

section Leatherworking 150-185

step Expert Leatherworking
  only Alliance
  zone Darnassus
  tip Expert Leatherworking raises the cap to 225; it needs skill 125 and level 20, and costs 50 silver. Telonis in Darnassus is the only Alliance Expert trainer. The Journeyman trainers still teach recipes until 150; past that you need the Expert trainers.
  level 20
  train Leatherworking Expert npc 4212

step Expert Leatherworking
  only Horde
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Expert Leatherworking raises the cap to 225; it needs skill 125 and level 20, and costs 50 silver. Una in Thunder Bluff is the only Horde Expert trainer. The Journeyman trainers still teach recipes until 150; past that you need the Expert trainers.
  level 20
  train Leatherworking Expert npc 3007

step Skin the Foothill Caverns Yetis
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip The Cave Yetis and Ferocious Yetis (level 30-32) inside the Foothill Caverns come back fast enough to stay inside the whole way to Skinning 225. If the cave is crowded, the Nightbane worgen around Roland's Doom and the Rotting Orchard in Duskwood are the alternative. Heavy Leather from these yetis is the entire 150-185 craft pile, and bonus Pristine Hide here is worth hoarding for later recipes.
  goto 43.3,31.2 "Cave Yeti, Ferocious Yeti" r 30
  goto 45.7,33.8 "Cave Yeti" r 30
  goto 45.2,28.4 "Ferocious Yeti" r 30
  goto 44.1,25.7 "Ferocious Yeti, Cave Yeti" r 30
  skill Skinning 225

step Leatherworking 150-185: vendor goods
  tip Fine Thread (50) for the shoulders and harness, and Silken Thread (10) for the gloves, from any Leatherworking Supply vendor.
  buy 2321 x50 nearest
  buy 4291 x10 nearest

step Leatherworking 150-185: Auction House
  tip What 150-185 takes that the Auction House sells: 293 Heavy Leather and 10 Iron Buckle. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 4234 x293
  auction 7071 x10

step Leatherworking 150-185: skinning
  tip Heavy Leather comes from beasts of level 28-40. Take it from your bags or bank after the Hillsbrad yeti loop above.
  collect 4234 x293 anywhere gather Skinning 140

step Barbaric Shoulders (150-165)
  tip Barbaric Shoulders, 15 to 165: 8 Heavy Leather, 1 Cured Heavy Hide and 2 Fine Thread each. These take 15 of the kept Cured Heavy Hides. The Journeyman trainers do not teach this recipe: learn it from the Expert trainers. Without the hides, buy Pattern: Barbaric Leggings from Jandia in Freewind Post (Horde) or Lardan in Astranaar (Alliance) and make 15 Barbaric Leggings (150 Heavy Leather, 15 Moss Agate, 30 Fine Thread) instead; buy the Moss Agate on the Auction House.
  learn 7151 "Barbaric Shoulders"
  craft 7151 "Barbaric Shoulders" until 165

step Guardian Gloves (165-175)
  tip Guardian Gloves, 10 to 175: 4 Heavy Leather, 1 Cured Heavy Hide and 1 Silken Thread each. These take the last 10 kept Cured Heavy Hides. Without the hides, start the Barbaric Harness at 165 instead (10 of them: 140 Heavy Leather, 20 Fine Thread, 10 Iron Buckle).
  learn 7156 "Guardian Gloves"
  craft 7156 "Guardian Gloves" until 175

step Barbaric Harness (175-185)
  tip Barbaric Harness, 10 to 185: 14 Heavy Leather, 2 Fine Thread and 1 Iron Buckle each. Blacksmiths make the Iron Buckles: buy them on the Auction House. If none are listed, make 10 Thick Armor Kits (50 Thick Leather, 10 Silken Thread) instead.
  learn 6661 "Barbaric Harness"
  craft 6661 "Barbaric Harness" until 185

section Leatherworking 185-235

step Artisan Skinning
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Artisan Skinning raises the cap to 300 and needs skill 200. Balthus Stoneflayer in Ironforge teaches it. Train it before the Thick Leather band so your skinning keeps climbing past 225.
  train Skinning Artisan npc 6291

step Artisan Skinning
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Artisan Skinning raises the cap to 300 and needs skill 200. Thuwd in Orgrimmar teaches it. Train it before the Thick Leather band so your skinning keeps climbing past 225.
  train Skinning Artisan npc 7088

step Artisan Leatherworking
  only Alliance
  zone The Hinterlands
  tip Artisan Leatherworking raises the cap to 300; it needs skill 200 and level 35. Drakk Stonehand at Aerie Peak, The Hinterlands, is the only Alliance Artisan trainer. Train it now: only the Artisan trainers teach the Nightscape Pants, and they take you to 235 but give no points past 225 without it. At 225 and level 40 the specializations open: Dragonscale, Elemental and Tribal. Each has its own quest chain; this guide does not route them.
  level 35
  train Leatherworking Artisan npc 11097

step Artisan Leatherworking
  only Horde
  zone Feralas
  tip Artisan Leatherworking raises the cap to 300; it needs skill 200 and level 35. Hahrana Ironhide at Camp Mojache, Feralas, is the only Horde Artisan trainer. Train it now: only the Artisan trainers teach the Nightscape Pants, and they take you to 235 but give no points past 225 without it. At 225 and level 40 the specializations open: Dragonscale, Elemental and Tribal. Each has its own quest chain; this guide does not route them.
  level 35
  train Leatherworking Artisan npc 11098

step Skin the Yetis (Feral Scar Vale)
  zone Feralas
  tip Feral Scar Yetis, Enraged Feral Scars and Hulking Feral Scars (level 43-46) pack the yeti cave at Feral Scar Vale in south Feralas. Horde come from Camp Mojache, Alliance from Feathermoon Stronghold. Work them to Skinning 275 and save every Thick Leather plus any Pristine Hide or Pristine Scale: the leather band ahead is large and the bonus drops are Forever's scarce skinning materials.
  goto 52.0,58.5 "Enraged Feral Scar, Feral Scar Yeti" r 30
  goto 50.6,58.8 "Hulking Feral Scar, Enraged Feral Scar" r 30
  goto 55.8,57.7 "Feral Scar Yeti" r 30
  goto 53.2,55.9 "Enraged Feral Scar, Feral Scar Yeti" r 30
  skill Skinning 275

